WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.032 --> 00:00:02.226
(exciting music)

00:00:02.226 --> 00:00:03.059
- [Boy] We didn't really have any

00:00:03.059 --> 00:00:05.860
fast stackers from Texas
until he came along.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:06.693
- [Boy] Like, I couldn't really

00:00:06.693 --> 00:00:08.914
believe my eyes. Like, I was in shock.

00:00:08.914 --> 00:00:10.052
- [Boy] His hands, like, they were

00:00:10.052 --> 00:00:12.408
always moving, and it was like, there was no, like,

00:00:12.408 --> 00:00:13.511
thinking about where to put it,

00:00:13.511 --> 00:00:16.386
it was just like a non-stop, just like

00:00:16.386 --> 00:00:17.276
(trilling)

00:00:17.276 --> 00:00:19.621
(drum beats)

00:00:19.621 --> 00:00:20.630
- [Boy] He's off the charts. He's

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.302
like as fast as a lightning bolt.

00:00:22.302 --> 00:00:24.718
(drum beats)

00:00:24.718 --> 00:00:27.385
(cups stacking)

00:00:35.851 --> 00:00:40.018
(gentle music) (cups stacking)

00:00:41.164 --> 00:00:42.459
- [Trey] My name is Trey Griffith,

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:43.521
and I'm the fastest cup stacker

00:00:43.521 --> 00:00:45.302
in the state of Texas. My goal

00:00:45.302 --> 00:00:49.103
is to be the fastest cup stacker
in the whole entire world.

00:00:49.103 --> 00:00:51.483
- [Carmen] When I first saw Trey

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:54.850
begin cup stacking, I was thrilled.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.231
Kids on the spectrum are always

00:00:56.231 --> 00:00:58.797
very passionate and very intense

00:00:58.797 --> 00:01:01.815
on what their fixation is. And he

00:01:01.815 --> 00:01:03.313
just shined. I mean, you could

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.113
see that he was in his element.

00:01:05.113 --> 00:01:07.863
He was comfortable, he was alive,

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.283
and he was just doin’ his thing.

00:01:14.238 --> 00:01:15.573
- [Jimmy] Trey took it to a completely

00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:17.292
different level. He was doing it

00:01:17.292 --> 00:01:19.358
systematically instead of just

00:01:19.358 --> 00:01:21.645
kinda for fun. And it was all

00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:24.815
about getting that next best time.

00:01:24.815 --> 00:01:27.462
What Trey does in five or six

00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:30.712
seconds, takes me 10 or 12, 13 seconds.

00:01:32.315 --> 00:01:35.322
We've learned not to ever discount

00:01:35.322 --> 00:01:37.572
what he says he's gonna do.

00:01:39.611 --> 00:01:40.767
(bright music)

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:44.110
- [Carmen] Sport stacking is using

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.001
a set of 12 plastic cups, and you

00:01:47.001 --> 00:01:50.168
stack them in a very specific sequence

00:01:51.163 --> 00:01:53.891
of pyramids, and you are racing

00:01:53.891 --> 00:01:57.060
yourself, and you're racing a timer.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:57.919
- [Jimmy] It's a sport that you

00:01:57.919 --> 00:01:59.428
don't have to be tall, you don't

00:01:59.428 --> 00:02:01.297
have to necessarily be able to

00:02:01.297 --> 00:02:03.167
run quickly. As long as you've

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:05.210
got the 12 cups, you've got a mat,

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.377
and you've got a timer, you can stack.

00:02:09.564 --> 00:02:12.327
To me, it's just mind-boggling

00:02:12.327 --> 00:02:14.324
to see these stackers like Trey

00:02:14.324 --> 00:02:16.402
and his friends. And you can tell

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.702
they're not even looking at the

00:02:17.702 --> 00:02:20.106
cups that they're stacking. It is

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:24.065
all muscle memory. I mean, it's so fast

00:02:24.065 --> 00:02:25.899
when they get to this level that

00:02:25.899 --> 00:02:28.743
the naked eye cannot see it all.

00:02:28.743 --> 00:02:32.910
(bright music) (cups stacking)

00:02:33.782 --> 00:02:35.326
When I found out that I was havin’ a boy,

00:02:35.326 --> 00:02:37.695
of course I thought about when I

00:02:37.695 --> 00:02:39.123
was a boy, and playing catch with

00:02:39.123 --> 00:02:41.410
my dad in the backyard, and you

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.848
flash forward, you know, thinking about

00:02:43.848 --> 00:02:46.182
those types of things with your kiddo,

00:02:46.182 --> 00:02:49.641
but when Trey found stacking, it was just like,

00:02:49.641 --> 00:02:53.101
okay, cool. Here is a
sport that he's into,

00:02:53.101 --> 00:02:55.226
and it's got speed; I've always loved

00:02:55.226 --> 00:02:57.536
sports with speed. And it's got rhythms,

00:02:57.536 --> 00:02:59.858
which make him happy. And I realized,

00:02:59.858 --> 00:03:02.099
what a better way to bond with my child,

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:04.746
than to learn how to stack myself.

00:03:04.746 --> 00:03:06.487
I get to stand next to my son, who's

00:03:06.487 --> 00:03:09.460
one of the fastest in the
world, and stack with him,

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.909
and be a part of something special.

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:14.022
- [Carmen] Watching the
two of them stack together,

00:03:14.022 --> 00:03:18.121
are probably some of the
best moments I've ever had.

00:03:18.121 --> 00:03:20.245
Our motto has always been: The family

00:03:20.245 --> 00:03:23.252
that stacks together, stays together.

00:03:23.252 --> 00:03:25.203
We go to these tournaments together,

00:03:25.203 --> 00:03:26.793
we’ve traveled together, we've made

00:03:26.793 --> 00:03:30.253
friends all over the
country, all over the world.

00:03:30.253 --> 00:03:33.260
I mean, it's definitely
enriched our lives.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.010
(cheerful music)

